       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, and the effects can last a long time because the half-life is 30\u201350 hours. Nothing about this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nPlease check whether one of these applies:\n- **Typo:** Did you mean 5 mg or 10 mg once daily?\n- **Different drug or unit:** Did you mean another medication, or a different unit?\n- **Intentional dose:** If you really want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd also suggest talking with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
